## Planning Mode Requirements

When working in **Planning Mode**:

- Always ask **at least 3 clarifying questions** before proposing a plan or implementation approach.
- Treat **any user comment sent while in Planning Mode** as a request to **update the previous plan** (revise the plan rather than starting over).
- Focus planning on producing **testable, human-readable, well-structured code** that a human can easily inspect.
- For this repository, planning must preserve these architectural invariants unless the user explicitly redefines them:
  - one episode equals one canonical simulation rollout,
  - train/eval/render consume the same simulation core outputs,
  - simulation owns physics/camera/reward computation while render is view-only,
  - `SimulationStateSeries` is the mandatory episode-level artifact.

## Ask When Unsure (No Guessing)

- If you are unsure whether to **extend existing code vs create something new**, ask the user instead of choosing.
- If you are unsure about **how/where to structure files and directories**, ask the user instead of assuming.

